build/
.caustic/
# Compiler output, and only compiler output. `caustic -c foo.cst` always emits
# `foo.cst.s`, so that suffix is the exact discriminator — a bare `.s` is a
# hand-written source the build links.
#
# This used to be `*.s` with an un-ignore per known file, which meant every NEW
# hand-written .s was silently untracked. kernel/random_asm.s was written, built
# locally, committed-around, and pushed missing; the branch it belonged to jumped
# to address 0 on the machine that checked it out, because the symbols it defines
# resolved to nothing. A rule you have to remember to update is a rule that
# eventually is not updated.
*.cst.s
*.o
.caustic-src/
.claude-docs/
# superpowers skill scratch (plans/specs) — keep local, never track
docs/superpowers/
# Python bytecode caches (e.g. scripts/png2csif.py → scripts/__pycache__/)
__pycache__/
